 ],
 "literal": "Listen! May you live long, O bee with beautiful wings! / There is no fear for a good word. If to his country's / majestic tall mountain you go, / where wild ginger is dense in the garden of beautiful small millet, / the younger sister of the weeders who strike with hoes raising fine dust, / \"She will not separate from her kin,\" please say so, to the lord of the mountain / where, like the fine leather shields of marching kings in a row, / honeycombs hang!",
 "translation": "Listen, may you live long, O bee with beautiful wings! There is no fear in speaking a good word. If you go to the majestic, tall mountain of his country—where the younger sister of the weeders, who raise fine dust as they strike with hoes in the small-millet field dense with wild ginger, will never separate from her kin—please say this to the lord of that mountain, where honeycombs hang like the fine leather shields of kings marching in a row.",
 "modern": "அழகிய சிறகுகளை உடைய தும்பியே! கேள், நீ டூழி வாழ்க! நல்ல வார்த்தையைச் சொல்வதற்கு எந்த அச்சமும் இல்லை. காட்டு இஞ்சி அடர்ந்த, அழகிய சிறு தினைப் புனத்தில், மண்வெட்டியால் கொத்தி நுண் துகளை எழுப்பும் களை எடுப்போரின் தங்கையான இவள், தன் சுற்றத்தாரை விட்டுப் பிரியமாட்டாள் என்று அவரிடம் சொல்வாயாக. அணிவகுத்துச் செல்லும் அரசர்களின் நுட்பமான தோல் கேடயங்களைப் போலத் தேன்கூடுகள் தொங்கும் மலைக்குத் தலைவனான அவனுடைய உயர்ந்த மலைக்கு நீ சென்றால், இதை அவனிடம் சொல்வாயாக.",
 "explanation": "The friend (தோழி) is speaking to a bee (தும்பி) in the hearing of the hero (தலைவன்) who is waiting nearby in secret. She asks the bee to carry a message to the lord of the mountain (the hero) when it flies back to his land. The message is that the heroine, described as the younger sister of the hardworking weeders in the millet fields, cannot live separated from her family. This is a subtle hint to the hero that he must marry her and take her with him properly, rather than continuing secret trysts. The image of honeycombs hanging like the leather shields of marching kings on the mountain slopes represents the wealth and strength of the hero's land, but also suggests that just as shields protect warriors, the hero must protect the heroine through marriage. This poem belongs to the Kuriñci (mountainous) landscape, where the wild ginger, millet fields, and honeycombs reflect the natural abundance of the hills.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
 "generated": "2026-11-26"
}